            <ArticleTitle>[Albumin metabolism in congestive circulatory insufficiency].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>94-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The examination was conducted in 78 patients with congestive circulatory insufficiency. Albumin metabolism was studied in these patients with the aid of 1(131)--labelled albumin after Metthews. The half-life of albumin was studied, as well as the decay speed factor and the synthesis rate. The plasma albumin level was determined. Changes in the half-life duration were revealed. Patients with Stage III dystrophic circulatory insufficiency were shown to have a reduced plasma albumin level, a shortened albumin half-life, and increased synthesis rate and decay factors. Patients with Stage II-A and B circulatory insufficiency had varying changes of these parameters differing from the normal range.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
